# Wednesday's rulings on the gate85 kit (KIT_REPORT.md §6), to be read WHOLE by the gate seat

Rulings carried from the gate84 kit (its RULINGS_wednesday.md including its "RULED at launch" block), from the gate84 VERDICT (`briefs_staged/2026-10-10_gate84_VERDICT.txt`), and from the task brief the gate85 kit builder was given (2026-10-11, the gate85 commission: "model it exactly on gate84", tier-1 gate on #1453, the gate decides the tier and must test the builder's measurements). Where this file is absent the gate uses the same defaults. Nothing below was invented by the kit builder except where a line says "NOT RULED" (and then it carries its DEFAULT). **There is NO "RULED at launch" block yet: Wednesday adds one (as she did for gate84, with a `.pre-launch` backup of this file).**

## Carried and still applying

- **The gate never edits, merges, comments on tickets or messages humans.** It never mails a builder seat. Its work ends at the verdict mail to Wednesday. It never edits the PR body: the LIVE body IS the builder's body here (sha256/16 `0e5b0383ca4e8c9c`, 11,296 B, round-trip identical at the raise); it is judged and reported, never changed. (gate82 / gate83 / gate84, unchanged.)
- **ONE verdict, GO or NO GO, at the pinned head (#1453).** A head that moved at the gate's START reading is **NOT RUN** (no verdict); a head that moves later voids the verdict. (gate84 wording kept.)
- **MERGE ADDENDUM, LAST in report.md:** one line for #1453 plus the composition line. The proposed squash subject carries **no `(#n)` suffix arithmetic**: the declared subject is the landed subject byte for byte, at most 92 characters as declared, and TRUE of the diff. (gate82 ruling, unchanged.)
- **Docs composition (carried from gate81..gate84, adapted to ONE PR):** #1453 appends flow block `57.` and a cheat section (KS-1432) immediately before the closing `</body>\n</html>\n` of the two platform-k HTML docs. At the draft develop (`4a7cc1f697f8`, the #1450 squash) already carries flow blocks in document order `... 50, 51, 52, 54, 53` (54 is KS-1434's, landed as `f8c86f859fe0`; 53 is #1450's, which sits after it in the file); the OPEN #1451 (KS-591) carries 55, the OPEN #1452 (KS-1364) carries 56, and #1383 (KS-1401) also touches the two docs. **While develop equals the base a plain merge of #1453 is clean (rc 0); once ANY of those lands first, the later PR conflicts at the shared line (1 hunk per doc) and the keep-both is the MERGE SEAT's job.** The gate proves it composable with a per-fragment COUNT (the matrix `html_docs_matrix.test.sh` cannot see a dropped block (gate81 G81-2) nor a DUPLICATED one (gate83 G83-1)). Renumbering is the merge seat's call.
- **Pre-existing CI (carried):** GitHub Actions IS EXECUTING on PRs (the CLAUDE.md "retired for billing" note is stale). `Security Scanning` (KS-1148: `Blockchain/Dev/scripts/audit/audit-locks.mjs` imports undeclared `semver`) is known; other reds are classified by JOB and STEP against develop's OWN push runs at the develop the gate reads. The gate **verifies every attribution** and does **not count a verified pre-existing red against any PR**. A red it cannot classify from the log BLOCKS. NOT RUN is never a pass; a run still in progress is UNMEASURED, never green.
- **An image-pull / infrastructure red (gate82 Q-INFRA1449, a single-instance pilot, NOT a standing rule):** the gate quotes the log line and says it cannot re-run a job; infrastructure is attributable only on that quoted evidence and stays UNPROVEN until the merge-in's own run is terminal.
- **Q-ATTR (carried):** the `Generated with` line is COUNTED and reported, not ruled (gate77 Q-ATTR77 precedent). The body carries 1.
- **Q-DOCKER (carried):** no Docker; the four platform suites NOT RUN / NOT COMMISSIONED (`docker info` once, quote rc, never start Docker).
- **Q-MODEL (carried):** the exec line carries no `--model`; Wednesday types `/model claude-opus-5-5` at the gate's idle prompt.
- **Q-CLASS / Q-HOOKS-SIBLINGS (carried):** a class sibling or a prediction slip found by the gate is reported only; Wednesday routes it via a board seat after a search. (The stale `CLAUDE.md` "Actions retired" note, `BACKLOG.md:674`, the stale tracking ref `refs/remotes/origin/develop` in the shared checkout: carried, unfiled. The shared checkout's local `develop` ref is also stale, which is why the hook printed the KS 991 notice on the builder's push.)
- **Kit defects gate84 found in its own kit (G84-1: c2 D5 used the DRAFT develop; G84-2: the cwd arm C5 was blind to commits and worktrees):** neither is repeated. Every gate85 instrument takes `--develop` as a REQUIRED argument (the develop the gate read), and the gate85 kit has no cwd/hook instruments.
- **Holds kept from gate84:** never touch the shared checkout's `core.hooksPath`; no board writes; findings only, never fixes; a suite that names env.example / bootstrap-env.sh is never run from inside a repo (none is run here at all).

