- **#1453 (KS-1432, C1), PROPOSED TIER 1 (census) by Seat F 14th; THE GATE DECIDES THE TIER** and must test the builder's measurements: the 16-value equivalence, the mutation table (M0 / M1 / M2), the red/green counts (test section alone 1 passed / 9 failed of 10; with the product 10/10; suite 869 -> 871) and the finding that the guard test does not see a deleted call site. Head `28a9c306a3b3622f8c376390ab6e75a637b6ee95`, parent = base = develop `4a7cc1f697f81f5b95d767dd5713ea344f3c76ea`. **No companion in the batch.**
- The kit's `route` instrument measures what the builder left UNMEASURED (array / number / string / boolean bodies through the real route with the check deleted); the kit's G4 mutation (call site weakened to `if (parsed === null)`) is ALL GREEN in the drafter's run. Both are PREDICTIONS; the gate re-measures.

## Not ruled by Wednesday (OPEN: each carries the kit's DEFAULT, to be confirmed or re-ruled)

- **Q-SEAT85 (merge seat): NOT RULED, NO DEFAULT IN THE FILES.** The launch command takes `--seat "Seat X nth"` and derives the GO string `GO (<seat>): merge 1453 on gate85`; the prompt carries the fill-at-launch token `@MERGE_SEAT@`. Nothing in the kit names a seat (the kit builder did not read which seats are alive; R 37th merged #1450 and its wrap state is Wednesday's read).
- **Q-TIER85 (verdict subject tag): NOT RULED. DEFAULT `GATE85 (T1)`** (the builder's proposal; THE GATE DECIDES, and records its own tier in a body line `TIER: ... (agreed | DISAGREE: reason)`; the subject stays `(T1)` so routing is mechanical). To change the tag edit `verdict_subject` in kit.json and the prompt, then run `pin_gate85.py`.
- **Q-NM85 (how the gate gets an installed node_modules): NOT RULED. DEFAULT: a read-only `cp -R` COPY from the builder's worktree `/Volumes/DevMASTER/!CODING/Secuura/Blockchain/worktrees/s-f14-c1/Blockchain/Dev` (node_modules + packages/shared/dist + services/api-gateway/node_modules), checked by `nmcheck` against the head's package-lock.json (0 mismatches required).** This is a named narrow exception to "never touch the builder's worktree" (X1): a READ, nothing is run in it. The shared checkout's own node_modules is STALE (57 version mismatches measured, `nmcheck` refuses it). The alternatives, both worse: `npm ci` (network, `~/.npm/_cacache`; gate82 G82-2 precedent) or a `--deps-from` pointing at a copy Wednesday prepares. **If the worktree is removed before the gate runs, the vitest-based checks are NOT RUN with the blocker named (never a pass).**
- **Q-BODY85 (does the gate read the body): NOT RULED. DEFAULT YES**, the LIVE body (it IS the builder's body), read-only, sentence by sentence, report only.
- **Q-STALE85 (a stale figure in the body): NOT RULED.** The kit reads ONE mismatch in the body's 31 checked figures: "Of the 11 changed lines in `verification.ts`, 0 match" (the final diff has +11/-1 = 12 changed lines; the 11 predates the comment line the builder added last). **DEFAULT: Polish, BLOCKS no**; the gate re-measures the pattern on the final bytes (the kit's F3: 0 of 12) and rules.
- **Q-SPARK85 (the false sentence in the committed test header): Wednesday already ruled (per the builder's READY): the Spark comment "uses [the predicate] at the POST /api/documents call site" is committed AS RECEIVED and FLAGGED UNVERIFIED in the body.** The gate rules its severity: the drafter's measurements (M2 and G4 both leave the guard test green) show the sentence is not true of THIS test. **DEFAULT: Minor, BLOCKS no (disclosed in the body); the gate states the true wording.** A reword is a follow-up, not the gate's.
- **Q-CALLSITE85 (the guard test cannot see the call site): the builder's own finding, a declared limit of C1.** The ticket's premise ("delete the real check and the suite stays green") is also not true at the base: M0 turns exactly one `ks815` cell red. **DEFAULT: Minor follow-up (a route-level cell for the four non-null shapes is a separate PR), BLOCKS no**; the gate rules, and says whether G4 (the call site weakened to null-only, ALL GREEN) changes the severity.
- **Q-HOOKRUN85 (no automatic runner):** neither CI nor the pre-push hook runs the api-gateway vitest suite (the raw push log names no `ks529` and no `vitest`; `ci.yml` is `workflow_dispatch` only). **DEFAULT: INFO, BLOCKS no**; the human runs the builder's test-block commands.
- **Q-STREAM85 (the test-block "stream parent"):** the builder did NOT determine which review stream, if any, carries KS-1432 (the ticket is on Kam's account); **Wednesday names it.** Not the gate's.
- **Q-DOCS85 (docs keep-both):** whichever of #1451 / #1452 / #1453 lands second needs the keep-both; **DEFAULT: the merge seat's, never the gate's or the author's.** The drafter read `merge-tree` rc 1 on exactly the two docs for #1453 vs each of #1451 and #1452.
- **Q-DEVCI85 / Q-DIRTYCI85:** the gate classifies develop's push-run reds (`pr`, `PR Security Gates`) by JOB and STEP at the develop it reads. The drafter read them at `4a7cc1f697f8`: `pr` = Akto [boot, enforce], Playwright [test:unit, upload], k6 [enforce, upload]; `PR Security Gates` = Code Security Gates [All shell test suites]; `Security Scanning` has no develop push trigger (comparators: other PRs' runs). A red it cannot classify from the log BLOCKS. This PR is NOT dirty (mergeable True, state unstable only while checks ran).
- **Q-PROMPT85:** the prompt has no drafter review beyond the kit's launcher `--check`. **Q-CHARTER85:** the kit builder READ the QA charter and BRIEF_TEMPLATE whole; STANDING_LINES.md was NOT read whole (the prompt's references to it are carried text).
- **Q-ARMS85:** the gate84 kit carried 185 refusal arms (`arms/`); the gate85 kit carries SELF-TESTS only (c1 46, c2 14, c3 27, gh 37) and the launcher `--check` refusal tests listed in KIT_REPORT §3. No arms driver was built (scale). **DEFAULT: accept.**
